.TH CLIPMAC 1 "September 2026" "Clip for Mac" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clipmac \- clipboard history that refuses to capture secrets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipmac
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command-line face of Clip for Mac. It reads the same history the app writes.
Items are addressed by position (1 = newest) or by stable id written as #12.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list [--limit N] [--pinned] [--json]
Recent items.
.TP
.B get \fIitem\fR
Print an item to stdout (image and file items print their bytes).
.TP
.B copy \fIitem\fR [--plain]
Put an item back on the pasteboard.
.TP
.B search \fIquery\fR [--limit N] [--semantic] [--json]
Full-text and substring search; --semantic adds on-device meaning matches.
.TP
.B pin \fIitem\fR [--keyword K] / unpin \fIitem\fR / snip \fIkeyword\fR / snippets [--export file.plist]
Pinned snippets. --export writes a macOS Text Replacement list.
.TP
.B pause [10m|1h] / resume
Pause capture; the menu bar icon shows the state.
.TP
.B forget \fIitem\fR | --app \fIbundle-id\fR | --sensitive
Real deletion, no undo.
.TP
.B wipe --yes
Delete everything, including pins.
.TP
.B assist "\fIquestion\fR" [--local | --cloud] [--last N | --today] [--yes] [--json]
Ask about recent items. --local uses Apple's on-device model. --cloud prints the redacted payload
and sends it only after confirmation (or --yes). \fBassist log\fR lists every cloud request.
.TP
.B status [--json]
Counts, FileVault, permissions, hotkey.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 fine, 1 warning, 2 problem, 64 usage error.
.SH FILES
~/Library/Application Support/Clip for Mac/history.db
.SH SEE ALSO
pbcopy(1), pbpaste(1)
